{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Basic_Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Basic Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Area)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Area)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Similar_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Similar Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb890e788c451fed032c8b221192c5ac43790206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e156331c13aae7e86644da6fa391b4389b826d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, and angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a right angle. A semicircle is inscribed in the triangle as shown. What is the radius of the semicircle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f66d4cef8b689eb626ec8c226380e1e72d8719.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(12,0)--(12,5)--(0,0)); draw(arc((8.67,0),(12,0),(5.33,0))); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (12,0), E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (12,5), NE); label(&quot;$12$&quot;, (6, 0), S); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, (12, 2.5), E);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6d82ac6e498c66fb6dae70f36f57315639d4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{7}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{13}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{59}{18}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{10}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can draw another radius from the center to the point of tangency. This angle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbcc051e4912bcdf1e6d4e347017eb00eaa85c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ODB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Label the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the point of tangency <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and the radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38fe1daab146801175ebc91b54d9343afa54e6b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(12,0)--(12,5)--(0,0)); draw(arc((8.67,0),(12,0),(5.33,0))); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (12,0), E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (12,5), NE); label(&quot;$12$&quot;, (6, 0), S); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, (12, 2.5), E); draw((8.665,0)--(7.4,3.07)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, (8.665, 0), S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (7.4, 3.1), NW); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (11, 0), S); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (7.6, 1), W); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/86336c38e566ee9aed996bcb23b696b87afed22b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ODBC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a kite, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f6b5fc25f72b810ef0c61d5a1f2e65e5d2c6cf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB=CB=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b7e8cdfa3785502cc330bc7be910b6bc11e12d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=13-5=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bbeb53280c838da30cc8e2c6d978045a3f8bfd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 + 8^2=(12-r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" />. Solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70fa84be524cbb7189da232c02225adfc3c2823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2+64=144-24r+r^2 \\Rightarrow 24r=80 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{10}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"393\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Basic_Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Basic_Trigonometry)\">Solution 2 (Basic Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Basic Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we reflect triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> over line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we will get isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we are capable of finding out that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ce2cd67d1e28e21b68f87f201f5034d2051f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c624d4ca633863e521200cce8afcab8f3786aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\frac{\\angle BAD}{2} = \\tan \\angle BAC = \\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"247\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, as of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, the radius of its inscribed circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84aae09fe513a1cc2de48ddef3592690b47da9e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{tan \\frac{\\angle BAD}{2}\\cdot (AB + AD - BD)}{2} = \\frac{\\frac{5}{12} \\cdot 16}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{10}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"442\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Bloggish\" title=\"User:Bloggish\">Bloggish</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 2, we reflect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> over line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and label the reflection of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ce2cd67d1e28e21b68f87f201f5034d2051f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" /> by the Pythagorean Theorem, we use the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f05229cd8000da5dcffd09d7301a10db11edc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=A$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the inradius (what we're trying to find), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the semiperimeter (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/75834e67664c46f1b3c126f46deb138f35edc188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\overline{AB}+\\overline{AD}+\\overline{BD}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" />), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the area of the triangle in which the incircle is inscribed in. Substitution gives: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/c/0cca9d38bb4f271a940ecb7477b7a5c5d21a029b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\frac{\\frac{10\\cdot12}{2}}{\\frac{13+13+10}{2}}\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/6773640f97cf9764864abdbcd4fb236d86ce40b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\frac{60}{18}\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140572b1fed069f81a8c8c070d8349a816452baa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{10}{3}}\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~megaboy6679\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Area.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Area)\">Solution 4 (Area)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Area)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the labels from Solution 1, we can express the area of the entire triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc6e55570b3fbd0c09a7216f8514f9e21828a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC] = [\\triangle ADO] + [\\triangle DBO] + [\\triangle OBC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"350\" height=\"20\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40acd8deb6fe683dab1feefa6002e81d81a40cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area_{\\triangle} = \\frac{1}{2}bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" /> for each term yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a39d12135382db430e17fc788809e6167f235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(AC)(CB) + \\frac{1}{2}(AD)(DO) + \\frac{1}{2}(BD)(DO) + \\frac{1}{2}(OC)(CB)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"468\" height=\"38\" />. By equal tangents, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/7251fd3e9de9faffe42bd11762f8626f4d120fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB = CB = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a904766b90b4980837f25de217c2058a35ca5d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"176\" height=\"21\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2e2df7e2d088858f4984f0a44646861001b7dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AB - DB = 13 - 5 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"243\" height=\"16\" />. Lastly, because both segments are radii of the semicircle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d001dc8513bc59c99ee6ba3ce24ed0f7f43134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD = OC = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging in, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/5380f869187d2de2e4aaa33f8247a5456d8bc5eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(12)(5) + \\frac{1}{2}(8)(r) + \\frac{1}{2}(5)(r) + \\frac{1}{2}(r)(5)\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"37\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9fba05b7e23245551de7899ce7ea498570978c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30 = 4r + \\frac{5}{2}r + \\frac{5}{2}r\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e9ec4e0bd70ae1c19acc24b3fee49078c58e77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30 = 9r\\]\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3cdb131a66d5e573ce5fbe9a81ad97b0c9394ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{10}{3}}\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~ yuzufufu\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Similar_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Similar_Triangles)\">Solution 5 (Similar Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Similar Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, we get the following diagram:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38fe1daab146801175ebc91b54d9343afa54e6b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(12,0)--(12,5)--(0,0)); draw(arc((8.67,0),(12,0),(5.33,0))); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (12,0), E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (12,5), NE); label(&quot;$12$&quot;, (6, 0), S); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, (12, 2.5), E); draw((8.665,0)--(7.4,3.07)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, (8.665, 0), S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (7.4, 3.1), NW); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (11, 0), S); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (7.6, 1), W); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p>We notice that since both triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/0448207f3062fba301e810680f612e359a51c623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> share angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, they are similar. Then we can say that (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f6b5fc25f72b810ef0c61d5a1f2e65e5d2c6cf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB=CB=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b7e8cdfa3785502cc330bc7be910b6bc11e12d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=13-5=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7aff7987f2ce92721b289e9a3de7e0fdc5e05225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{AC} = \\frac{OD}{CB} \\Rightarrow \\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{r}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"39\" />. Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a374bae492657e2f6dc2dd5f7ecd99607806f5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{40}{12} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{10}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"151\" height=\"49\" />. ~nidharshana29\n</p><p>P.S: Full credit for the unedited asymptote goes to MrThinker who made it in Solution 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy!)\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qZJNi-WM0XY?si=AL2FANuanWBAQu17\">https://youtu.be/qZJNi-WM0XY?si=AL2FANuanWBAQu17</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KtmLUlCpj-I\">https://youtu.be/KtmLUlCpj-I</a> \n</p><p>- savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sOF1Okc0jMc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sOF1Okc0jMc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 8\">2017 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Prec